      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Town Creek’s first post office opened in 1837, marking the town’s early development after settlers arrived in the 1830s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/town-creek/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town officially incorporated in March 1875, establishing its municipal government after decades of growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
